# A declared array size between INT_MAX and LONG_MAX. is_int accepts it --
# it fits in a long and is positive -- but gman::InlineParse::get_size must
# still refuse it with RIE_RANGE rather than let static_cast<int> turn it
# negative. Declare alone only adds to the dictionary and would exit 0; the
# crash (today, an uncaught std::bad_alloc, SIGABRT) happens where a request
# *uses* the token and GMANParameterList sizes an allocation from the
# resulting negative quantity, so this fixture uses "big" the way
# tests/rib/malformed/declare_array_overflow.rib uses "hugearray".
#
# A trailing Sphere follows AGENTS.md's "RIB authoring" section, "The
# desync convention."
Declare "big" "constant float[3000000000]"
Display "malformed_out.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 200 200 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.6]
Surface "plastic" "big" [1.0]
Sphere 0.5 -0.5 0.5 360
WorldEnd
